Specification Shopping Cart



Background Catalog 
Given catalog has: Catalog
| Name        | Price |
| Widget      | 10    |
| WhatCallIt  | 20    |
| ThingaMaJig | 30    |

Entity CatalogItem 
| Attribute | Type       | Default | Notes |
| Name      | SimpleText | NoName  |       |
| Price     | Dollar     | 1       |       |

Collection Catalog
| DataType    | Minimum | Maximum  | Notes          |
| CatalogItem | 0       | 10000000 | Each is unique |


Entity  OrderItem 
| Attribute | Type       | Default | Notes |
| Name      | SimpleText | No Name |       |
| Quantity  | Integer    | 1       |       |
| Price     | Dollar     | 1       |       |
| ItemTotal | Dollar     | 1       |       |

Collection OrderItemCollection
Description Collection of Items 
| DataType  | Minimum | Maximum | Notes                     |
| OrderItem | 0       | 100     | Should no have duplicates |

Scenario Add items
Given item collection is : OrderItemCollection
| Name | Price | Quantity | ItemTotal |
When item added : OrderItem Vertical 
| Name     | Widget |
| Quantity | 2      |
Then item collection is : OrderItemCollection 
| Name   | Price  | Quantity | ItemTotal |
| Widget | $10.00 | 2        | $20.00    |
When item added : OrderItem Vertical 
| Name     | WhatCallIt |
| Quantity | 3          |
Then item collection is : OrderItemCollection
| Name       | Price  | Quantity | ItemTotal |
| Widget     | $10.00 | 2        | $20.00    |
| WhatCallIt | $20.00 | 3        | $60.00    |

 
Entity Address 
# will update the individual types later 
| Name   | Type       | Default | Notes |
| Street | SimpleText |         |       |
| City   | SimpleText |         |       |
| State  | SimpleText |         |       |
| ZIP    | SimpleText |         |       |

Define NoAddress = 
| Street | City | State | ZIP |
|        |      |       |     |

Entity ShoppingCart 
| Name            | Type                | Default    | Notes |
| Items           | OrderItemCollection | =EmptyCart | No    |
| Shipping        | Dollar              | $0         |       |
| Discount        | Dollar              | $0         |       |
| TotalPrice      | Dollar              | $0         |       |
| ShippingAddress | Address             | =NoAddress |       |
| BillingAddress  | Address             | =NoAddress |       |

Define ABillingAddress = 
| Street       | City      | State | ZIP   |
| 1 Apple Lane | Somewhere | NC    | 27705 |

Define AShippingAddress = 
| Street       | City      | State | ZIP   |
| 2 Apple Lane | Somewhere | NC    | 27706 |

Scenario   A ShoppingCart with Addresses
Given shopping cart : ShoppingCart
| ShippingAddress   | BillingAddress   | Items      |
| =AShippingAddress | =ABillingAddress | =EmptyCart |








Define EmptyCart 
| Name | Price | Quantity | TotalPrice |

Define TwoItemCart
| Name       | Price  | Quantity | TotalPrice |
| Widget     | $10.00 | 2        | $20.00     |
| WhatCallIt | $20.00 | 3        | $60.00     |

Scenario Add items to Shopping Cart 
Uses Discount, Shipping_Cost
Given shopping cart : ShoppingCart
| Items      | Shipping | Discount | TotalPrice |
| =EmptyCart | $0       | $0       | $0         |
When item added : OrderItem Vertical 
| Name     | Widget |
| Quantity | 2      |
When item added : OrderItem Vertical 
| Name     | WhatCallIt |
| Quantity | 3          |
Then shopping cart is : ShoppingCart
| Items        | Shipping | Discount | TotalPrice |
| =TwoItemCart | $5       | $4       | $81        |

Scenario Cost of Empty OrderItemCollection
Given item collection : OrderItemCollection 
| Price | Quantity | TotalPrice |
When total computed 
Then result is: Pricing  
| TotalPrice |
| $0         |

Attributes Pricing
| Attribute  | DataType |
| TotalPrice | Dollar   |


BusinessRule Shipping_Cost 
Description How much to charge for shipping 
Examples: Shipping
| Total Price | Shipping Cost | Notes                |
| $99.99      | $5.00         | Less than $100       |
| $100.00     | $0            | Free if $100 or more |

Attributes Shipping
| Attribute     | DataType |
| Total Price   | Dollar   |
| Shipping Cost | Dollar   |
| Notes         | String   |

BusinessRule Discount 
Description how much discount to give
Examples: Discounting
| Total Price | Discount | Notes |
| $24.99      | 0        |       |
| $25.00      | 5        |       |
| $99.99      | 5        |       |
| $100.00     | 10       |       |

Attributes Discounting
| Attribute   | DataType   |
| Total Price | Dollar     |
| Discount    | Percentage |
| Notes       | String     |

DataType Percentage 
Description  standard percentages 
Uses Decimal 
Examples: ValidValues
| Value | IsValid | Notes |
| 0     | y       |       |
| 99    | y       |       |
| 100   | y       |       |
| 101   | n       |       |
| -1    | n       |       |




